        <mxCell id="seq3-1" value="3 · Rendering a tool part: two data paths to the same service" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="16" width="671" height="32" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="seq3-2" value="execute gave Claude up to 20 rows to reason over (page 2). The table in the answer fetches its own rows through the REST API, like the Users page,&lt;br&gt;so it pages, sorts and authorizes the same way. The tool input is the page's query: apart from title, every field is a /users URL parameter.&lt;br&gt;Code: frontend/src/features/assistant/components/chat-message.tsx, tool-part-view.tsx, list-tool-card.tsx, tool-bodies/users-body.tsx,&lt;br&gt;lib/tool-renderers.ts · frontend/src/features/users/components/users-table.tsx · backend/src/features/users/users.controller.ts&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Notation:&lt;/b&gt; solid line, filled head = call · open head = asynchronous or streamed message (SSE) · dashed = return · narrow bars = activation&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Colours:&lt;/b&gt; blue = browser (React) · green = API (NestJS) · orange = Claude (Anthropic API) · grey = PostgreSQL" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=12;fillColor=#fdfdfd;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="58" width="960" height="98" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
